1
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:10,000
He who holds the sword, rules the world.

2
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Prince Valiant is a adventure, fantasy film directed by Anthony Hickox.

3
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:18,000
An Arthurian legend of young Prince Valiant, son of the King of Scandia.

4
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:22,000
After the King is exiled by an evil leader, the Prince travels to Camelot to secure the aid of King
Arthur in helping restore his family to power and prevent a plot by the Black Knight.

5
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Prinz Eisenherz, played by Stephen Moyer.

6
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Princess Ilene, played by Katherine Heigl.

7
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:34,000
Thagnar, played by Thomas Kretschmann.

8
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:38,000
King Arthur, played by Edward Fox.

9
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Sligon, played by Udo Kier.

10
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Morgan Le Fey, played by Joanna Lumley.

11
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:50,000
Prince Valiant is a 1997 independent sword and sorcery film directed by Anthony Hickox, written by Michael Frost Beckner,
and starring Stephen Moyer, Katherine Heigl, Thomas Kretschmann, Joanna Lumley, Ron Perlman, and Edward Fox.

12
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
It is a loose adaptation of the long-running Prince Valiant comic strip of
Hal Foster, some panels of which were used in the film.

13
01:18:52,000 --> 01:18:58,000
In it, Valiant must battle the Vikings and a
scheming sorceress to save the kingdom.

14
01:24:56,000 --> 01:25:02,000
The film explores themes of princess, sword,
prince, camelot, vikings (norsemen).
